% Evidence against an exception, derived by a rule.
% The exception injured(a) has 0.6 for it; the vet rule derives 0.58
% against it. Both are tested against one shared number, so injured(a)
% holds without conflict only in a share of 0.6 - 0.58 = 0.02, and only
% there does it block the default. gk answers flies(a) with (.98, 0, 0, .02),
% the same value the fact 0.58::-injured(a) would give.
bird(a).
0.6::injured(a).
vet(a).
0.58::-injured(X) :- vet(X).
flies(X) :- bird(X), unless(injured(X), 2).
query(flies(a)).
